Subject: [PATCH] jails/instances/lab-mail: Sync the Next and Later folders
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab@lists.p7x.dev
Change-Id: xlunvnzsqsvlpvpmzoomywrowwpymvzx
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:52:12 +0000

Pat triages the list in three steps, not two: a message is either
done, needs work soon, or can wait. INBOX and Archive alone cannot hold
that middle state anywhere every client and agent sees it, and a
notmuch tag cannot either, since it is not in the list data and a
rebuilt index loses it.

Next and Later are folders like Archive, so the state travels with the
message through lab-mail and Fastmail. The spec makes the folder the
only state: clients derive their tags from it, and a move is the one
way to change it, from Emacs or Fastmail's web interface alike.

The spec also turns flag sync on for Pat's notmuch, so read, flagged,
and answered match Fastmail and notmuch serves as a full client of the
account. It stays off for the agent, whose login cannot set flags.
