This applies on top of "[PATCH v8 0/9] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build
the list's mail hub" [1], which sets the fixed folder list this patch
extends.

It changes lab-mail and its spec only. The client side the spec now
describes, mail-tag.sh deriving next, later, and archived from the
folder and an Emacs command that moves the file, belongs with moving
beastie's notmuch off the jj maildir. Until then those clients still
read ~/lab/mail.jj, where flag sync must stay off.

Before the first sync, create Next and Later on Fastmail; mbsync
creates no folder.

Not tested on a running jail: doveconf is not installed on my host,
so the two mailbox blocks are checked only against the existing ones.

